{"id": "EUVD-2026-97440", "enisaUuid": "60add6ce-9b3b-31fb-96fa-58ec0582fc49", "description": "LogicalDOC Community Edition through 9.3 contains an unauthenticated file upload vulnerability in the UploadServlet that allows remote attackers to write files to disk without a session. Attackers can repeatedly send multipart requests with unlimited file parts to /upload, persisting files in uncleaned temporary directories and exhausting server disk space.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T13:39:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T17:49:18", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/logicaldoc/community/discussions/119", "https://github.com/logicaldoc/community/commit/90b7ebea5330feab94aff5ef0573362f3e52a1cc", "https://github.com/logicaldoc/community/blob/9.3/logicaldoc-webapp/src/main/java/com/logicaldoc/web/UploadServlet.java#L128", "https://github.com/logicaldoc/community", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/logicaldoc-community-edition-through-9.3-unauthenticated-upload-disk-exhaustion-via-uploadservlet"], "aliases": ["GHSA-528h-c74g-p276", "CVE-2026-109205"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.42, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c4e47b52-9c6a-3084-9f35-daee018b49de", "product": {"name": "LogicalDOC Community Edition", "vendor": {"name": "LogicalDOC"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22649.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2b9f873d-34cd-318a-a371-0ce5781b2673", "vendor": {"name": "LogicalDOC"}}], "isExploited": false}